      "designInstructions": "**Serif/Sans Split** — Display headlines use an editorial serif (Instrument Serif) for warmth and literary authority. All body text, UI elements, and navigation use a geometric sans (DM Sans). This split communicates that Claude thinks in humanities but operates in technology.\n\n**Cream Parchment Canvas** — The surface system runs on warm cream tones: #FAF9F5 (base), #F5F4ED (secondary), #F0EEE6 (tertiary). Pure white (#FFFFFF) appears only on elevated cards and inputs. The cream palette gives every page a handmade, paper-like warmth that rejects the cold whites of typical tech products.\n\n**Clay-Coral Brand Signal** — The primary clay-coral (#C96442) appears on the brand CTA button and key interactive elements. It reads as warm terracotta rather than urgent red. A mineral green (#629987) provides complementary accent for secondary highlights and illustrations.\n\n**Border-Thickening Hovers** — Interactive elements respond to hover by thickening their borders from 1px to 2px, creating a tactile \"pressing into\" the surface effect. No shadows are added on hover. The border change is the primary interactive feedback.\n\n**Tonal Card Elevation** — Cards elevate by shifting from the cream base to pure white (#FFFFFF). Borders use warm greys (#D1CFC5, #E8E6DC) at fine 1px weights. Pricing cards are the only elements that use a subtle shadow, earned through their commercial importance.\n\n**Fluid Clamp Typography** — Font sizes use CSS clamp() for fluid scaling between breakpoints. Display sizes range from 72px to 30px across viewports. The sizing is continuous rather than stepped, matching the organic warmth of the palette.\n\n**Hand-Drawn Illustration Style** — Illustrations use a hand-drawn, slightly imperfect line quality with the clay/mineral/oat palette colors. They reinforce the humanist positioning — technology that feels crafted rather than manufactured.\n\n**Multi-Color Pictogram Accents** — The extended palette includes oat (#E3DACC), peach (#EBC9B7), fig (#C46686), cactus (#BCD1CA), sky (#6A9BCC), and heather (#CBCADB) — used for pictogram backgrounds and decorative elements. Each color is desaturated and warm.\n\n**Mood** — The warmest AI design system. Literary, humanist, handcrafted. A parchment library where intelligence feels like wisdom rather than computation.",
      "id": "style_8d06e6aab52b",
